  "policies": {
    "program": "Independent next_spell_adjacent, consumed by the next accepted payload of any real CAST origin; countered/no-target failures do not accept a payload.",
    "neighbors": "Capture the complete original physical board before the primary text. Keep immediate left/right minion allocations; locations block adjacency. Execute the primary body, then left/right bodies. Each extra target must retain its original presence and pass ordinary spell target legality immediately before execution; never retarget or bridge.",
    "payload": "Repeat the complete original ordered on_play body vector, original branch/conditions, ongoing payload and Twinspell derivative through the existing shared spell payload. Preserve one physical CAST, one hand play/payment and one finished event. Damage, Overload, summons and all non-target portions execute for each legal extra body. Current multi-arrow/group-target spell receipts are explicitly rejected before commit, pending dedicated body proof support; ordinary targetless/hero/minion paths remain executable. Dynamic one-cost Potion recipes now preserve two ordered ingredient steps and a finish per original physical/adjacent body, each bound to its original body acceptance/completion window. Components remain ordinary effects, not separate casts.",
    "save": "Original program material, board, full body identities, ordered private start/finish facts and shared cursor persist through choice/clone/replay/rollback. CAST target history remains the original arrow; a running body uses its own captured target.",
    "boundaries": "Original exact-presence policy, base-left-right order, all-CAST payload acceptance, countered retention, multi-target spells and interactions with rewinds/repeat auras remain local policies pending CN calibration. No client/AI/version-alignment blocker."
  },
  "uncertainties": [
    "Official 29.2 establishes ordinary target legality. Exact timing/stacking and physical transform/control/re-entry boundaries are local policies, not official calibration.",
    "Full past Legendary transform dependencies remain open. Complete Shaman71 stays unbound; no executable-subset pool is created. Version/hotfix alignment and rule-edge calibration are deferred.",
    "YOG_522 remains partial: actual BE_302 multi-arrow body proofs remain open; secondary-target listener/memory semantics remain separately unverified. Dynamic one-cost Potion bodies are internally implemented, not a CN calibration claim."
  ],
